WHAT IS DECIDED (do not reopen)
- Rules decide only for NEW names (git semantics): a tracked path stays recorded.
- Built-ins:
  - a `.git` component;
  - FIFOs and sockets (S3 builds them; until then mknod of either keeps answering EPERM);
  - anything under an untracked directory;
  - inside a nested repository: any directory above the name, other than the tree's root, holding a `.git` entry, while Nested::Exclude.
- Operator rules: `-agentfs` (info/attributes) and info/exclude.
- Tree `.gitignore` and `.gitattributes` files are ordinary content.
- The rule files are `<state>/history.git/info/exclude` and `<state>/history.git/info/attributes`. They are read once in `TreeActor::serve`, before any write. A missing file is empty; an unreadable one fails the open.
- Untracked files are plain passthrough files: no close-to-open, no journal, never gated by the history lag gate.
- A fork starts with an empty area. The area is removed when the fork drops.

